       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen at 5000 mg per dose, or 15 g/day, is a potentially lethal dose. A single dose over about 150 mg/kg, or roughly 10 g for a 70 kg adult, is in the range where hepatotoxicity is a concern. I can't think of a clinical situation where this order would be safe.\n\nHere are some other options:\n- **Standard dosing:** I can enter 650 mg or 1000 mg by mouth every 6\u20138 hours, with a daily maximum of 4 g (or less if you prefer).\n- **Dose typo:** If you meant a different number, such as 500 mg, tell me and I'll enter it.\n- **Possible overdose:** If you're concerned about an ingestion, I'd suggest contacting poison control and starting your hospital's acetaminophen toxicity protocol. That is a different order set from this one.\n- **Pharmacy review:** If you think there's a special indication, pharmacy or toxicology can review it with you first.\n\nWhat would you like me to enter?"
      }
